IN THE SUPREME COURT OF INDIA
CASE NO: Criminal Appeal No. 200 of 2024
CITATION: 2024 SCC OnLine SC 1920
YEAR: 2024

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: B.R. Gavai, K.V. Viswanathan

PARTIES:
Manish Sisodia vs Enforcement Directorate

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Prevention of Money Laundering Act, 2002, Constitution of India

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 45 PMLA, Article 21

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
speedy trial, prolonged undertrial detention, article 21 over statutory bar

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Ruled that where an accused has suffered prolonged custody and trial delay without fault, constitutional liberty under Article 21 takes precedence over statutory bail restrictions under Section 45 PMLA.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 45 PMLA, Article 21.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

